 "text": "Hi, how are you doing these days? Think of it like memory and storage. An SSD gives much faster access to the information you already have on it, while a hard drive gives you much more space at a lower price. Yes, it's quite something. You can copy large photo albums across in few minutes, or move every file to an SSD for smooth startups. A typical 32 MB SSD is reasonable now, and going to four times that gets quite pricey. Cloud is great for files you have everywhere, like documents and photos, and it gets much cheaper perbyte years ago. An SSD on the other hand beats it for speed any time you access a file.",
